# NOT A SECRET — safe to commit, safe to share, safe for every teammate's clone.
#
# Local stack only. `supabase start` loads this file into every Edge Function's
# environment automatically (a fixed Supabase CLI convention — this path cannot be
# renamed and still be picked up). It is committed, not gitignored, precisely so the
# whole team gets a working local stack straight out of `git clone` with no manual
# per-developer setup step.
#
# Why the value below is not a secret:
#   - It resolves to "pooler", the Docker hostname of the LOCAL Supavisor container —
#     reachable only from inside this repo's own docker compose network, never from
#     the internet.
#   - Its password is a fixed, public, local-only string. supabase/seed.sql resets it
#     to this exact value on every `supabase db reset`, so it is never a real secret
#     to protect or rotate — same category as the "postgres"/"postgres" superuser
#     credentials `supabase status` already prints for this project's local DB_URL.
#   - It authenticates nothing beyond this throwaway local Postgres, which this
#     project's own tooling destroys and recreates from migrations at will.
#
# This is NOT the platform's own SUPABASE_DB_URL (a direct, unrestricted connection).
# ADR-0009 needs a connection through Supavisor in transaction mode, authenticating as
# the privilege-free `edge_functions` role rather than as an owner.
#
# A deployed project's real EDGE_DB_URL is a genuine secret and must never look like
# this file: it is set with `supabase secrets set EDGE_DB_URL=...` by an operator, held
# only in that Function's platform secrets, and never written to any file this or any
# other repo tracks.
EDGE_DB_URL=postgresql://edge_functions.pooler-dev:edge-functions-local-dev-only@pooler:6543/postgres
